MID_EV14_018_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_018_m01_001: You're leaving already, Leilidahna?
MID_EV14_018_m01_002: Yes. I've taken advantage of your kindness\nfor too long.
MID_EV14_018_m01_003: And I want to get to Dagsion as soon as possible.\nMy plan hasn't changed. I have to see it through.
MID_EV14_018_m01_004: Besides, the timing is good. The attention stirred up\nby those wanted posters faded while we were here.
MID_EV14_018_m01_005: But more than anything, I want to settle the score\nwhile that man is still in Dagsion.
MID_EV14_018_m01_006: Ah, that reminds me... The Heroic Games are\nscheduled to begin today.
MID_EV14_018_m01_007: <NCA>Show surprise and confusion.
MID_EV14_018_m01_008: What? No...that means—
MID_EV14_018_m01_009: It means that even if we leave now, we'll never make\nit in time.
MID_EV14_018_m01_010: There's no need to panic. You'll arrive in plenty of\ntime if you use the Gate of the Gods.
MID_EV14_018_m01_011: What's that?
MID_EV14_018_m01_012: Oho! It's a convenience, you might say. A very\nspecial feature built right into the temple.
MID_EV14_018_m01_013: Those who use it can travel from here to Dagsion\ninstantaneously!
MID_EV14_018_m01_014: Whoa, I had no idea something like that existed!\nHave you ever used it, Olympia?
MID_EV14_018_m01_015: No, uh...I have not yet tried it myself.
MID_EV14_018_m01_016: Interesting. I wouldn't have thought we'd gain access\nto the Gate of the Gods so easily.
MID_EV14_018_m01_017: Leilidahna, before you leave for Dagsion, I want\nyou to promise me one thing...
MID_EV14_018_m01_018: Whatever happens, you must not sacrifice yourself to\nkill your target. You must survive and return to me.
MID_EV14_018_m01_019: The Heroic Games are a year-long event. And\ntruthfully, I do not much like the sight of blood.
MID_EV14_018_m01_020: But I must make an appearance as a show of\ndeference to the Divine Sovereign...my brother.
MID_EV14_018_m01_021: Since I'm on my way there anyway, I thought we\nmight all take a journey through the Gate together.
MID_EV14_018_m01_022: Kalla...I don't understand. Why would you go to\nso much effort on my behalf?
MID_EV14_018_m01_023: I know that my actions on behalf of one insignificant\nhuman may seem extravagant...
MID_EV14_018_m01_024: But Leilidahna, please understand. I see my beloved\nchild, Cohen, in you.
MID_EV14_018_m01_025: Oh, wow... Does that mean that the goddess Kalla\nherself is the mother of Leda's...ancestor?
MID_EV14_018_m01_026: Fascinating. The legendary bard's origins have always\nbeen a mystery, but this explains many things.
MID_EV14_018_m01_027: I am sorry. I don't mean to make you feel as though\nyou must be some kind of substitute for my son.
MID_EV14_018_m01_028: Still, I would like to do whatever I can to help you.
MID_EV14_018_m01_029: I...understand. I accept your assistance with\nhappiness and gratitude.
MID_EV14_018_m01_030: I do have a favor to ask in return.
MID_EV14_018_m01_031: I would like to reveal the true architects behind the\nCydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_018_m01_032: This is why I sent Syracusio to infiltrate the kingdom\nof Arago. I wanted him to begin an investigation.
MID_EV14_018_m01_033: As a member of House Cohendia, you are intimately\ntied to what happened in Cydonia.
MID_EV14_018_m01_034: So, if you're willing, I would like you to assist in\nthis work.
MID_EV14_018_m01_035: <NCA>Agree to her request.
MID_EV14_018_m01_036: I see. Yes, I would like that very much.
MID_EV14_018_m01_037: It may be that your quest for revenge helps us\nreveal the heart of the matter.
MID_EV14_018_m01_038: Please use Syracusio in whatever manner you see fit.\nAnd do let me know as soon as you learn something.
MID_EV14_018_m01_039: Now, it is time to depart for Dagsion. Everyone,\nfollow me.
MID_EV14_068_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_068_m01_001: You lose, kid. Don't get me wrong—you've got talent,\nno doubt about it. But you've got a long way to go.
MID_EV14_068_m01_002: You're no ordinary man, are you?
MID_EV14_068_m01_003: Kill him! You there, sir? KILL HIM!
MID_EV14_068_m01_004: That man is a monster. Execute him. Do it at once!
MID_EV14_068_m01_005: You would not dare defy an order from Gilchris I,\nking of Arago!
MID_EV14_068_m01_006: Is it gold you want? Is that what it is?
MID_EV14_068_m01_007: It's yours! More than you'll make in a lifetime.\nWhat's your price?
MID_EV14_068_m01_023: Ohhh! The White-Maned Demon casts his eyes\non me... Fine. I'll do it myself!
MID_EV14_068_m01_024: Time to put him down like the rabid cur he is. Here I\ncome, little doggy!
MID_EV14_068_m01_025: His Majesty is exhausted from the journey. Soldiers,\nwould you escort the royal couple to their chambers?
MID_EV14_068_m01_026: Wait, let me go! Bertrand!
MID_EV14_068_m01_008: You must survive. And you must keep asking\nyourself what it is you lack.
MID_EV14_068_m01_009: By the time we next meet, have those combat skills\nof yours polished to a high shine. Understand?
MID_EV14_068_m01_010: Who are you? The way you handle that sword—\nit's strikingly familiar.
MID_EV14_068_m01_011: Hmmm.
MID_EV14_068_m01_012: Ahh... What a magnificent fight. Wouldn't you\nagree, Babbu?
MID_EV14_068_m01_013: Though I admit the lack of bloodshed was a\nterrible disappointment.
MID_EV14_068_m01_014: Still, one doesn't often see the White-Maned Demon\nbacked into a corner like that.
MID_EV14_068_m01_015: He may have been defeated, but he performed as\nexpected. The Demon's skills cannot be denied.
MID_EV14_068_m01_016: I suppose I really am starting to like that man.
MID_EV14_068_m01_017: Hrm...
MID_EV14_068_m01_018: Heeheehee! Perhaps I should get rid of you and let\nthat delicious demon tend to me instead.
MID_EV14_068_m01_019: Please, Lady Iliana, do not say such things,\neven in jest!
MID_EV14_068_m01_020: And you do not talk back to me, Yanjin. I will not\ntolerate insolence from the likes of you.
MID_EV14_068_m01_021: Give me a chance to prove to you that I am,\nin all ways, superior to him.
MID_EV14_068_m01_022: Hmm...what an interesting proposal.
MID_EV14_019_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_019_m01_001: Milady, the man in that match... There's something\ndifferent about him. But he is the man you seek.
MID_EV14_019_m01_002: I know exactly who he is.
MID_EV14_019_m01_003: If I could jump down from here and plunge my blade\nstraight into Bertrand's chest, I would.
MID_EV14_019_m01_004: My goodness, Leilidahna! You are acting very\nstrange. Please, do calm down.
MID_EV14_019_m01_005: So this is the man you spend all of your time\nthinking about. I admit I'm a little jealous.
MID_EV14_019_m01_006: It's strange... He seemed to be staring at something—\nor perhaps someone—in the audience.
MID_EV14_019_m01_007: Yes, he did...
MID_EV14_019_m01_008: Ah! Is that—
MID_EV14_019_m01_009: Those seats are reserved for Arago's nobility. But it\nseems the king and his entourage have departed.
MID_EV14_019_m01_010: Speaking of Arago, it's said that Bertrand murdered\nthe king.
MID_EV14_019_m01_011: Murdering a king doesn't just...happen. Surely there's\nsomething there between him and the royal family.
MID_EV14_019_m01_012: Haaah... Haaah... Haaah...
MID_EV14_019_m01_013: Leda, you don't look so good.
MID_EV14_019_m01_014: Is she...hyperventilating? What in the heavens is\nwrong with you, Leilidahna?
MID_EV14_019_m01_015: Sirocco, who is that man with the vicious look\nin his eyes?
MID_EV14_019_m01_016: Based on his demeanor and access to the royal seats,\nhe could be the captain of the king's guard.
MID_EV14_019_m01_017: I've never met him myself, but if memory serves,\nhe has a rather bad reputation.
MID_EV14_019_m01_018: He is notoriously cruel, so much so that he's called\nthe Mad Dog by those who work with him.
MID_EV14_019_m01_019: He's been with Gilchris since the king was just a\ngeneral. He reportedly got his start as a foot soldier.
MID_EV14_019_m01_020: He was given some sort of important assignment and\nthen abruptly rose to captain of the king's guard.
MID_EV14_019_m01_021: Lechner...
MID_EV14_019_m01_022: What was that? Miss Leda...what did you say?
MID_EV14_019_m01_023: Ah...
MID_EV14_019_m01_024: Milady! What's the matter?!
MID_EV14_019_m01_025: This will not do! We must take her somewhere quiet!
MID_EV14_019_m01_026: I'm sorry... I must have fainted.
MID_EV14_019_m01_027: Leilidahna, you began acting strangely the moment\nyou laid eyes on that man.
MID_EV14_019_m01_028: I know him. That's Lechner. I'm sure of it.
MID_EV14_019_m01_029: Hey, that's the last name on your revenge list, right?\nThe Mahdel List?
MID_EV14_019_m01_030: I remember him so clearly now. A few days before\nthe invasion...I met him.
MID_EV14_019_m01_031: I...I let him into Kassite...by accident.
MID_EV14_019_m01_032: Let him in? Miss Leda...what do you mean?
MID_EV14_019_m01_033: How could I have forgotten about this?
MID_EV14_019_m01_034: Kassite had closed its gates. We were afraid the army\nfrom Arago might invade.
MID_EV14_019_m01_035: I saw him crawl out of a canal that brought water in\nfrom outside the walls. He was breathless and scared.
MID_EV14_019_m01_036: I should have reported him to a nearby soldier, but...
MID_EV14_019_m01_037: He was so desperate... He begged me not to tell\nanyone. So I didn't.
MID_EV14_019_m01_038: Later, I spotted the same man I'd helped. This time,\nhe was standing on top of a watchtower...
MID_EV14_019_m01_039: He laughed as he fired an arrow at the generals from\nArago who'd gathered outside our walls.
MID_EV14_019_m01_040: His arrows gave the soldiers a reason to raid Kassite\nthat day and led to every terrible thing that followed.
MID_EV14_019_m01_041: After his attack, the soldiers poured into town,\nleaving nothing but devastation in their wake.
MID_EV14_019_m01_042: And it was all my fault. I didn't report him...\nI should have reported him...
MID_EV14_019_m01_043: This connection to the captain of the king's guard is\nvery unexpected.
MID_EV14_019_m01_044: I've committed a terrible sin. What I did is...\nunforgivable. And now I wonder if I...
MID_EV14_019_m01_045: I focused all of my hatred on Bertrand so I could\nforget what I did... Pretend it wasn't all my fault.
MID_EV14_019_m01_046: Milady, you were just a child at the time. You can't\nblame yourself for this.
MID_EV14_019_m01_047: I'm sorry. I need to be alone.
MID_EV14_019_m01_048: I'm going to take a walk around the city. I'll return to\nthe temple after I clear my head.
MID_EV14_020_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_020_m01_001: That was quite harrowing. I can't thank you enough\nfor coming to my aid.
MID_EV14_020_m01_002: Oh, don't worry. It was nothing. I was in a bad mood\nanyway. That was just the distraction I needed.
MID_EV14_020_m01_003: You know, you don't seem like someone who'd spend\ntheir time slumming in this part of town.
MID_EV14_020_m01_004: Oh, uh, no, no. I am a perfectly normal young woman\nwho grew up in this part of town like...normal.
MID_EV14_020_m01_005: Listen—it's none of my business, and I'm not going\nto make it my business. So you can drop the act.
MID_EV14_020_m01_006: Do I...really seem so out of place here?
MID_EV14_020_m01_007: You really do. Let's just say you don't seem very\ncomfortable in a neighborhood of this...caliber.
MID_EV14_020_m01_008: A-ah!
MID_EV14_020_m01_009: Oh, please excuse me. I haven't eaten\nanything today.
MID_EV14_020_m01_010: Let me guess... You don't have any money on you?
MID_EV14_020_m01_011: Yes, well, I was in a hurry to depart. And it just\nslipped my mind, I suppose.
MID_EV14_020_m01_012: A perfectly normal young woman with a perfectly\nnormal set of problems. I think I know what to do...
MID_EV14_020_m01_013: That's enough of that.
MID_EV14_020_m01_014: Thank you so much. We've only just met, and yet\nyou've been so kind to me.
MID_EV14_020_m01_015: And the way you play—it's simply extraordinary.\nI've never heard anything like it.
MID_EV14_020_m01_016: You have to be joking. Someone like you must have\nall the most skilled musicians at her beck and call.
MID_EV14_020_m01_017: I do know someone who's reputed to be a very skilled\nplayer, but...
MID_EV14_020_m01_018: I've never had a chance to listen to them. Perhaps\nI never will.
MID_EV14_020_m01_019: Hmm, why is that? You don't get along or something?
MID_EV14_020_m01_020: Yes, that's probably the best way to put it.
MID_EV14_020_m01_021: But listen, I have heard some good performances,\nand still none have come close to yours today.
MID_EV14_020_m01_022: Heh. I guess I'll just have to accept your\ncompliment, then.
MID_EV14_020_m01_023: There's someone else who I know would appreciate\nhearing your music. But that isn't possible now.
MID_EV14_020_m01_024: <NCA>Show interest.
MID_EV14_020_m01_025: <NCB>Let it go.
MID_EV14_020_m01_026: <ACA>Oh? Someone you're close to?
MID_EV14_020_m01_027: <ACA>Yes, but...also no. I can't see him anymore. He's too\nfar away, in a place I can't reach him.
MID_EV14_020_m01_028: <ACA>He was in trouble once and needed me to believe in\nhim. But I didn't. I've regretted it ever since.
MID_EV14_020_m01_029: <ACA>Now I want so very badly to save him—to atone for\nmy terrible mistake and to make things right.
MID_EV14_020_m01_030: <ACA>I understand. I have so many regrets. Sometimes\nI think it would be easier to just...let go and die.
MID_EV14_020_m01_031: <ACA>But no matter how hard things get, we humans have\nto find a reason to go on living.
MID_EV14_020_m01_032: <ACA>Yes, you're right... You're exactly right.
MID_EV14_020_m01_033: You know, we've been here quite a while.\nIs that OK? Are you expected anywhere?
MID_EV14_020_m01_034: Oh no! I mean yes, I really must go.
MID_EV14_020_m01_035: Thank you so much for today, Leda. I will never\nforget what you've done for me.
MID_EV14_020_m01_036: You saved me, fed me, and you even played music\nfor me.
MID_EV14_020_m01_037: Leda, I hesitate to ask anything more of you, but I'd\nbe honored if I could count you as a friend.
MID_EV14_020_m01_038: I'm embarrassed to admit it, but I don't have many\nfriends my age.
MID_EV14_020_m01_039: Really? Um, yes. I'll be your friend, if that's what\nyou want. I'd like that.
MID_EV14_020_m01_040: Thank you, Leda. That pleases me very much.
MID_EV14_021_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_021_m01_001: Kalla, I heard you wanted to see me. What can\nI do for you?
MID_EV14_021_m01_002: Ah, here you are, Leilidahna. I've just heard from the\nadministrators of the Heroic Games.
MID_EV14_021_m01_003: It would seem your match is scheduled to take place\ntwo months from now.
MID_EV14_021_m01_004: That means a lot of free time for us, huh?
MID_EV14_021_m01_005: It does. Milady, we should use this time to our\nadvantage.
MID_EV14_021_m01_006: Kalla, goddess of mine heart, your favorite\nmischievous breeze has just blown in.
MID_EV14_021_m01_007: And Miss Leda, you're here. Perfect timing.
MID_EV14_021_m01_008: Ah, Syracusio. I haven't seen you for some time.\nTell me—what whispers arrive on the wind?
MID_EV14_021_m01_009: Well, I've been looking into people with ties to Arago,\nand inquiring about Lechner...
MID_EV14_021_m01_010: You said something about "perfect timing." Did you\nlearn something?
MID_EV14_021_m01_011: Why, yes, I did. I learned some very helpful\ninformation, in fact.
MID_EV14_021_m01_012: It seems Lechner spends most of his time in the\nguesthouse for visitors from Arago.
MID_EV14_021_m01_013: He keeps watch over the king there, which means he\nwon't be easy to get to.
MID_EV14_021_m01_014: True. I wonder if there's a way to lure him out.
MID_EV14_021_m01_015: Ah, but wait, Miss Leda—I haven't gotten to the\nmost interesting part yet.
MID_EV14_021_m01_016: While Lechner is the captain of the king's guard,\nhe arrived in the city well before the royal family.
MID_EV14_021_m01_017: In fact, rumor has it he came to Dagsion about\na year ago.
MID_EV14_021_m01_018: Wait, so...he's the captain of the king's guard but\nwasn't actually guarding the king all that time?
MID_EV14_021_m01_019: Yes, and about once a month, he sneaks out of\nDagsion to go...somewhere.
MID_EV14_021_m01_020: It's said that when he returns, he has plenty of\ncash to throw around too.
MID_EV14_021_m01_021: Sadly, I don't yet know what these mysterious outings\nare about, though it can't be anything respectable.
MID_EV14_021_m01_022: Hmm, I'm impressed. You uncovered a lot of very\ngood information.
MID_EV14_021_m01_023: Yes, my investigation methods do tend to...uncover...\ngood things. Surely my many collaborators agree.
MID_EV14_021_m01_024: I don't get it?
MID_EV14_021_m01_025: And you shouldn't. You're still a bit too young, Mu.
MID_EV14_021_m01_026: Oh, Syracusio, one of these days you will end up\nstabbed to death in some woman's bed.
MID_EV14_021_m01_027: And what a happy death that will be. Far better than\nbleeding out in some lonely corner of a battlefield.
MID_EV14_021_m01_028: Oh, really? I cannot say I agree with that sentiment.\nNot at all.
MID_EV14_021_m01_029: Back to Lechner—you said he sneaks out of the\nguesthouse once a month?
MID_EV14_021_m01_030: Do these outings seem to be connected to some kind\nof event or pattern?
MID_EV14_021_m01_031: Excellent question, Miss Leda. They do.\nI've examined which days he's gone...
MID_EV14_021_m01_032: and it seems he always departs just before the\nnew moon arrives.
MID_EV14_021_m01_033: So, I think we can expect that he'll make his next\nmove around the same time.
MID_EV14_021_m01_034: What say we lie in wait for him then? We can follow\nhim at a distance and see where he goes.
MID_EV14_021_m01_035: I say I like this plan.
MID_EV14_021_m01_036: And if he happens to wander off by himself, I'll\nkill him right then and there.
MID_EV14_021_m01_037: Oh, Leilidahna...
MID_EV14_100_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_100_m01_001: Hmm?!
MID_EV14_100_m01_002: Obsidian is...resonating with something.
MID_EV14_100_m01_003: Wait...is one of Drake's treasures nearby? Is this\nlike that time with Balboa?
MID_EV14_100_m01_004: If so, it might mean someone's following me. I've got\nto figure out what's going on.
MID_EV14_100_m01_005: Though it's strange—this doesn't feel like a typical\nresonance. Have I...felt this from Obsidian before?
MID_EV14_100_m01_006: Hmm... Dhaba's Compass is reacting. One of\nDrake's treasures must be close.
MID_EV14_100_m01_007: Very close... I hope they're reasonable,\nwhoever has it.
MID_EV14_100_m01_008: Oho! Pardon me, miss.
MID_EV14_100_m01_009: Do you need something from me?
MID_EV14_100_m01_010: I can't imagine what I could possibly need when\nall that's beautiful in the world is right here.
MID_EV14_100_m01_011: I was looking for something interesting, and\nyou caught my eye. Serendipity, I'm sure.
MID_EV14_100_m01_012: Or was it fate? It does feel like fate, doesn't it?
MID_EV14_100_m01_013: {SetColor=Gray}Ugh. A flirt. Just what I need right now. But at\nleast he's not following me.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_100_m01_014: The name's Talimun. I'm a merchant of some\nsuccess and renown. And you are?
MID_EV14_100_m01_015: Leda. And I am just an ordinary bard. Obviously.
MID_EV14_100_m01_016: Yes, I see you have a vihuela. I've always been\ndrawn to lady vihuela players...
MID_EV14_100_m01_017: My mother was a master of the vihuela,\nor so I've been told.
MID_EV14_100_m01_018: Say, you aren't my mother, are you? And this,\nour fated reunion?
MID_EV14_100_m01_019: Ah, so you're a terrible flirt, and you have an awful\nsense of humor. Your mother would be proud.
MID_EV14_100_m01_020: I have to ask... What is that thing in your mouth?
MID_EV14_100_m01_021: Oh, it's cinnamon. It helps me stay sharp,\nyou see.
MID_EV14_100_m01_022: Cinnamon is hard to find...and expensive! And you\nwalk around chewing on it like a cow chews its cud?
MID_EV14_100_m01_023: Hm? Oh, I'm incredibly rich. There's plenty of my\nmoney to go around. Speaking of which...
MID_EV14_100_m01_024: Let me take you to this place I know. We can sample\ntheir finest ghosh, get to know each other... My treat.
MID_EV14_100_m01_025: Then who knows. Maybe I can listen to you play that\nvihuela... Or perhaps I'll end up playing your strings.
MID_EV14_100_m01_026: Please stop. If this is your idea of a pickup line,\nthe answer is no.
MID_EV14_100_m01_027: I'm so very not in the mood.
MID_EV14_100_m01_028: Talimun! There you are... I need explanations for\nthese unaccounted-for expenses.
MID_EV14_100_m01_029: Damn... Sorry—something's just come up.
MID_EV14_100_m01_030: Maybe some other time... Until then!
MID_EV14_100_m01_031: Talimun—stop! Apologies, miss.
MID_EV14_100_m01_032: He was an awful flirt, but I have to admit...it felt\nlike there was something more to him.
MID_EV14_100_m01_033: He was outgoing and confident, but it's a mask for\nsomething he keeps hidden, way below the surface.
MID_EV14_100_m01_034: Ugh, not again. Why am I such a magnet for men\nlike this?!
MID_EV14_022_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_022_m01_001: It's just as we predicted, Miss Leda. Lechner is\non the move.
MID_EV14_022_m01_002: The new moon is almost here. Looks like you had\nthe right of it.
MID_EV14_022_m01_003: But why did he pick this time of month? It's so dark\nit's hard to go anywhere or do anything.
MID_EV14_022_m01_004: Is that not the entire point? This is the perfect time\nfor a man like him to do his lurking!
MID_EV14_022_m01_005: He certainly does not want to be seen doing\nwhatever it is he's doing...understand?
MID_EV14_022_m01_006: <NCA>Suggest you find an opening to kill him.
MID_EV14_022_m01_007: <NCB>Suggest you follow and watch.
MID_EV14_022_m01_008: <ACA>The moment Lechner steps off the beaten path, I'm\ngonna choke the life from him.
MID_EV14_022_m01_009: <ACA>About that. If I may, I recommend we wait and\nwatch a spell... See what he does.
MID_EV14_022_m01_010: <ACA>You're telling me that I should pass on an opportunity\nto take my revenge?
MID_EV14_022_m01_011: <ACA>You must keep a level head, Miss Leda. Your chance\nwill come. You don't have to rush toward it.
MID_EV14_022_m01_012: <ACB>We don't want to be seen either. A moonless night\nlike this means we can follow him without notice.
MID_EV14_022_m01_013: <ACB>Killing him will have to wait until after we find out\nwhat he's up to.
MID_EV14_022_m01_014: <ACB>You're right. It's unlikely he'll spot us in\nthis darkness.
MID_EV14_022_m01_015: But listen...doesn't something about all of this seem\nsuspicious to you?
MID_EV14_022_m01_016: Even if those people on the Mahdel List did strike\nthe match that set Cydonia ablaze...
MID_EV14_022_m01_017: Do you really think that particular cast of characters\ncould have pulled it off?
MID_EV14_022_m01_018: You are dancing around the issue, Syracusio. Just say\nwhat you mean.
MID_EV14_022_m01_019: What I'm saying is anyone can dream up ambitious\nschemes. But to make them real? That takes acumen.
MID_EV14_022_m01_020: Whatever's at play here is too vast and complicated\nto have been masterminded by that motley band.
MID_EV14_022_m01_021: For it to play out exactly as planned...imagine\nthe luck they would have needed!
MID_EV14_022_m01_022: So...you think someone else has been controlling the\npeople on the Mahdel List?
MID_EV14_022_m01_023: That's exactly what I think, Mu. Smartly observed.
MID_EV14_022_m01_024: Kalla herself said she wants to get to the truth\nbehind the Cydonia Massacre, did she not?
MID_EV14_022_m01_025: I believe there's a key piece that's still hiding\nsomewhere in the shadows.
MID_EV14_022_m01_026: If we follow Lechner, we'll get a better idea about\nwho's behind all of this...
MID_EV14_022_m01_027: That's what you think?
MID_EV14_022_m01_028: For now, that is my theory, yes. Let's follow him and\nfind out if I'm right.
MID_EV14_022_m01_029: Fine. But we have to move now before we lose sight\nof him.
MID_EV14_023_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_023_m01_001: Doesn't look like anyone lives in this mansion.\nThe yard is full of weeds...
MID_EV14_023_m01_002: Why would Lechner come here?
MID_EV14_023_m01_003: Sirocco, is it wise to come this far inside\nthe grounds?
MID_EV14_023_m01_004: You can relax. We are downwind of our quarry.
MID_EV14_023_m01_005: As long as you remain quiet, they won't notice us.
MID_EV14_023_m01_006: Hm? *sniff* That fragrance... Ambergris from the\nsouthern sea?
MID_EV14_023_m01_007: <NCA>Look around.
MID_EV14_023_m01_008: Mu...you see that thing sitting there in the dark?\nLooks familiar, doesn't it?
MID_EV14_023_m01_009: Oh no! It's the ghost carriage?! What's it doing here?
MID_EV14_023_m01_010: If you're here, then something must be wrong.\nWhat is it?
MID_EV14_023_m01_011: A strange man has been prowling around recently.\nSo, I'm taking every precaution.
MID_EV14_023_m01_012: I'll be accompanying you from here on to ensure\nnothing happens to our cargo.
MID_EV14_023_m01_013: Yeah, well, here's this month's delivery. Would you\nlike to check it over?
MID_EV14_023_m01_014: Yes, I would.
MID_EV14_023_m01_015: It all seems to be here.
MID_EV14_023_m01_016: Of course it is. You think I'd pocket a few pieces for\nmyself, do you?
MID_EV14_023_m01_017: Here's your payment—one hundred thousand gold,\nas usual.
MID_EV14_023_m01_018: You know, this stuff we're hauling goes for 10 million\ngold. Maybe more! That's a lot of gold, yeah?
MID_EV14_023_m01_019: I can't help but think you could sweeten the deal\na bit, eh, boss?
MID_EV14_023_m01_020: I mean, here we are, two good friends sharing the\nburden of a secret. And friends do help friends.
MID_EV14_023_m01_021: Lechner, let me ask you... Do you want to live a long\nlife? If so, I wouldn't be so greedy if I were you.
MID_EV14_023_m01_022: Alright, alright. Guess I can't win with you.
MID_EV14_023_m01_023: Let's get this onto the ship at once. Quickly now,\nall of you.
MID_EV14_023_m01_024: Yessir!
MID_EV14_023_m01_025: We must depart as soon as they've finished.
MID_EV14_023_m01_026: So Lechner is connected to the ghost carriage.\nI didn't see that coming.
MID_EV14_023_m01_027: The boxes they're taking off of the carriage seem to\nbe traveling onward by ship.
MID_EV14_023_m01_028: If what Lechner said is true, a cargo worth 10 million\nin gold is very disquieting.
MID_EV14_023_m01_029: What I want to know is who were the other two\npeople—the woman and that bandaged man?
MID_EV14_023_m01_030: All I know is they were super creepy.
MID_EV14_023_m01_031: Hmm, I didn't recognize the bandaged man either.\nI would certainly remember someone like that.
MID_EV14_023_m01_032: As for the woman, it was too dark for me to see her\nclearly, but she has also piqued my curiosity.
MID_EV14_023_m01_033: Gods, she was as terrifying as ever. Thought she'd\nnever leave.
MID_EV14_023_m01_034: As for you night crawlers, how long did you plan to\nworm about in the dark, listening in?
MID_EV14_023_m01_035: Goodness me, you knew we were here? Should\nI be impressed?
MID_EV14_023_m01_036: Well, well, aren't you a beauty. How unexpected.\nBeautiful and full of murderous rage, I see.
MID_EV14_023_m01_037: With all that anger oozing from your pretty pores,\nI bet you weren't really trying to hide, were you?
MID_EV14_023_m01_038: Hehehehe!
MID_EV14_023_m01_039: At last we meet! Gods, I have been trying to find you\nfor SUCH a long time.
MID_EV14_023_m01_040: And now that we've finally met, I'm afraid I can't let\nyou go. Not again. Not you, Lechner Milloy.
MID_EV14_023_m01_041: They call you the Mad Dog of Arago because you're\nso very brutal, isn't that right?
MID_EV14_023_m01_042: You're the one who snuck into Kassite right before\nthe Cydonia Massacre...
MID_EV14_023_m01_043: You stood atop the city walls and rained arrows\ndown upon the generals of the Aragonian army.
MID_EV14_023_m01_044: You made it seem like Cydonia had attacked first,\ngiving those generals an excuse to invade.
MID_EV14_023_m01_045: You even made sure Menza Stronghold couldn't\nclose its gates and protect the city.
MID_EV14_023_m01_046: How do you know so many details, hmm? Did\nsomeone go and tell tales on me?
MID_EV14_023_m01_047: Whatever. Your corpse will be all the answer I need.
MID_EV14_024_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_024_m01_001: I think we're finally safe. I doubt that crew would\nfollow us this far.
MID_EV14_024_m01_002: I don't understand. Who were those people?
MID_EV14_024_m01_003: I don't know, but they were very skilled.
MID_EV14_024_m01_004: No ordinary fighters, indeed. They were as adept as\nvulkans, though surely not imperial soldiers.
MID_EV14_024_m01_005: My theory: they're some kind of elite force under the\nking of Arago's command.
MID_EV14_024_m01_006: The king is said to have a band of bodyguards called\nthe Order of the Haze.
MID_EV14_024_m01_007: Damn, damn, DAMN. How could I miss my chance\nto kill Lechner? He was right in front of me...
MID_EV14_024_m01_008: I should have been stronger...more powerful.
MID_EV14_024_m01_009: If I had been, I would have crushed his skull and sent\nhim straight into the depths of the underworld!
MID_EV14_024_m01_010: If this is the best I can do, I won't stand a chance\nagainst Bertrand!
MID_EV14_024_m01_011: Leilidahna, please! Seeing how we all made it out\nalive, perhaps you should see this for the win it is.
MID_EV14_024_m01_012: More importantly, we know that Lechner can be\nfound in Dagsion, do we not?
MID_EV14_024_m01_013: Another opportunity will present itself. For now, we\nbide our time and sharpen our claws.
MID_EV14_024_m01_014: Ah...
MID_EV14_024_m01_015: What is it? Did I say something wrong?
MID_EV14_024_m01_016: No... You said something very sensible. I guess\nI hadn't expected that from you.
MID_EV14_024_m01_017: What?! What, exactly, are you implying?
MID_EV14_024_m01_018: Aw, it's so nice when they get along.
MID_EV14_024_m01_019: Yes, it is. I don't remember the last time I saw milady\nlike this... Being friendly with someone her own age.
MID_EV14_024_m01_020: Oh, Buccar, you don't have to cry.
MID_EV14_024_m01_021: There are still so many unknowns. But here's what\nwe do know...
MID_EV14_024_m01_022: The ghost carriage smuggles a mysterious cargo into\nDagsion with Lechner as its ever-watchful guard.
MID_EV14_024_m01_023: A strange man in bandages and a mysterious woman\nthen take that cargo...somewhere across the lake.
MID_EV14_024_m01_024: It's hard to follow it all.
MID_EV14_024_m01_025: I agree. There are so many strange new characters all\nof a sudden. The story has gotten quite confusing.
MID_EV14_024_m01_026: With everything that's happened...maybe this plot\nreally does run deep, after all?
MID_EV14_024_m01_027: Yes, I think it does. I also think it's time to take\neverything we've uncovered to Kalla.